# Tor optimized for Iranian networks - Tor 0.4.9.11
# This torrc must sit NEXT TO tor.exe. All paths are relative, so the whole
# folder is fully portable: copy/move it anywhere and it still works.

# --- Local proxies (Windows system proxy uses HTTP 8118) ---
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050
HTTPTunnelPort 127.0.0.1:8118
DNSPort 127.0.0.1:53530
ControlPort 127.0.0.1:9051
HashedControlPassword 16:AA4A310F3B7F257A600E2B2959FEF3C5168E32655ED2919426B7D82CA5
SocksPolicy accept 127.0.0.1
SocksPolicy reject *

# --- GeoIP (next to tor.exe; needed for country-based options) ---
GeoIPFile geoip
GeoIPv6File geoip6

# --- Bootstrap/circuit tuning (verified to reach 100% from a clean state) ---
# NOTE: do NOT add ConfluxEnabled or ExitNodes/StrictNodes here - they were
# proven to stall bootstrap at 45-50% even with a working binary.
DormantOnFirstStartup 0
DormantCanceledByStartup 1
LearnCircuitBuildTimeout 0
CircuitBuildTimeout 30
MaxCircuitDirtiness 1800
NumEntryGuards 15
NumDirectoryGuards 6
MaxClientCircuitsPending 64
TokenBucketRefillInterval 10 msec

# --- Pluggable transports (same folder as tor.exe; used only when bridges are configured) ---
ClientTransportPlugin webtunnel exec webtunnel.exe
ClientTransportPlugin obfs4 exec obfs4proxy.exe
ClientTransportPlugin snowflake exec snowflake-client.exe

# --- Operational (data\ folder is created next to tor.exe automatically) ---
DataDirectory data
Log notice file data\tor.log
DisableDebuggerAttachment 1
AvoidDiskWrites 1
SafeLogging 1

# --- Bridges (optional) ---
# Direct connection works on most networks. If your network blocks Tor, run
# scripts\fetch-bridges.ps1 - it refreshes bridges and adds UseBridges 1 +
# Bridge lines to this file.
